<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<title>Mortgage Interest Credit Form</title>
<style>
  @page { size: A4; margin: 0; }
  .page {
    width: 794px; height: 1123px;
    padding: 50px 60px; box-sizing: border-box;
    overflow: hidden; page-break-after: always;
    position: relative;
    font-family: "DejaVu Serif", "Liberation Serif", Georgia, "Helvetica", Arial, sans-serif;
  }
  .page:last-child { page-break-after: auto; }
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; }
  td { padding: 4px 0; }
  .header-row td { padding-top: 10px; padding-bottom: 10px; }
  .section-title { font-weight: bold; margin-top: 15px; margin-bottom: 5px; }
  .sub-section-title { font-weight: bold; margin-top: 10px; margin-bottom: 3px; }
  .instruction { font-size: 0.9em; line-height: 1.4; }
  .caution { border: 1px solid #000; padding: 10px; margin-top: 10px; font-size: 0.9em; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="page">
  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start;">
    <div>
      <h1 style="font-size: 24pt; margin: 0;">8396</h1>
      <p style="margin-top: 10px;">Department of the Treasury</p>
      <p>Internal Revenue Service</p>
      <p>Name(s) shown on your tax return</p>
    </div>
    <div style="text-align: right;">
      <div style="font-size: 10pt;">OMB No. 1545-0074</div>
      <div style="font-size: 10pt;">2007</div>
      <div style="font-size: 10pt;">Attach to Form 1040 or 1040NR. <span style="font-weight: bold;">&#9658;</span> See instructions on back.</div>
      <div style="font-size: 10pt;">Sec. No. 138</div>
      <p style="margin-top: 20px;">Your social security number</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2 style="font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 20px;">Mortgage Interest Credit</h2>

  <div style="margin-top: 20px;">
    <p class="instruction">Enter the address of your main home to which the qualified mortgage certificate relates if it is different from the address shown on your tax return.</p>
    <!-- Address fields would go here if present -->
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 20px;">
    <p class="instruction">Name of Issuer of Mortgage Credit Certificate Mortgage Credit Certificate Number Issue Date</p>
    <table style="width: 100%;">
      <tr class="header-row">
        <td style="width: 40%;"></td>
        <td style="width: 30%;"></td>
        <td style="width: 30%;"></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><span data-field="issuer_name">{{ issuer_name }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="certificate_number">{{ certificate_number }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="issue_date">{{ issue_date }}</span></td>
      </tr>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h3 style="font-size: 12pt; margin-top: 25px;">Part I Current Year Mortgage Interest Credit</h3>
  <table style="width: 100%; margin-top: 10px;">
    <thead>
      <tr class="header-row">
        <td style="width: 10%;"></td>
        <td style="width: 60%;"></td>
        <td style="width: 15%;"></td>
        <td style="width: 15%;"></td>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>1</td>
        <td>Enter paid on the certified indebtedness interest. If someone else (other than your spouse if filing jointly) also held an interest in the home, enter only your share of the interest paid</td>
        <td><span data-field="amount_1">{{ amount_1 }}</span></td>
        <td></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>2</td>
        <td>Enter the certificate credit rate shown on your mortgage credit certificate. Do not enter the interest rate on your home mortgage</td>
        <td><span data-field="rate_2">{{ rate_2 }}</span></td>
        <td>%</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>3</td>
        <td>If line 2 is 20% or less, multiply line 1 by line 2. If line 2 is more than 20%, or you refinanced your mortgage and received a revised certificate, see the instructions for the amount to enter.</td>
        <td><span data-field="amount_3">{{ amount_3 }}</span></td>
        <td></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>4</td>
        <td>You must reduce your deduction for home mortgage interest on Schedule A (Form 1040) by the amount on line 3.</td>
        <td></td>
        <td></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>5</td>
        <td>Enter any 2004 credit carryforward from line 16 of your 2006 Form 8396</td>
        <td><span data-field="carryforward_2004">{{ carryforward_2004 }}</span></td>
        <td></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>6</td>
        <td>Enter any 2005 credit carryforward from line 16 of your 2006 Form 8396</td>
        <td><span data-field="carryforward_2005">{{ carryforward_2005 }}</span></td>
        <td></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>7</td>
        <td>Enter any 2006 credit carryforward from line 19 of your 2006 Form 8396</td>
        <td><span data-field="carryforward_2006">{{ carryforward_2006 }}</span></td>
        <td></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>8</td>
        <td>Add lines 3 through 6</td>
        <td><span data-field="sum_3_to_6">{{ sum_3_to_6 }}</span></td>
        <td></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>9</td>
        <td>Enter the amount from Form 1040, line 46, or Form 1040NR, line 43</td>
        <td><span data-field="amount_1040">{{ amount_1040 }}</span></td>
        <td></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>10</td>
        <td>1040 filers: Enter the total of the amounts from Form 1040, lines 47 through 49 and lines 51 and 53; line 12 of the line 11 Worksheet in Pub. 972 (see instructions); and Form 5695, line 15</td>
        <td><span data-field="amount_1040_filers">{{ amount_1040_filers }}</span></td>
        <td></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>11</td>
        <td>1040NR filers: Enter the total of the amounts from Form 1040NR, lines 44, 46 and 48; line 11 of the line 11 Worksheet in Pub. 972 (see instructions); and Form 5695, line 15</td>
        <td><span data-field="amount_1040nr_filers">{{ amount_1040nr_filers }}</span></td>
        <td></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>12</td>
        <td>Subtract line 9 from line 8. If zero or less, enter -0 here and on line 11 and go to Part II</td>
        <td><span data-field="subtraction_9_from_8">{{ subtraction_9_from_8 }}</span></td>
        <td></td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h3 style="font-size: 12pt; margin-top: 25px;">Part II Mortgage Interest Credit Carryforward to 2008. (Complete only if line 11 is less than line 7.)</h3>
  <table style="width: 100%; margin-top: 10px;">
    <thead>
      <tr class="header-row">
        <td style="width: 10%;"></td>
        <td style="width: 60%;"></td>
        <td style="width: 15%;"></td>
        <td style="width: 15%;"></td>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>12</td>
        <td>Add lines 3 and 4</td>
        <td><span data-field="add_3_and_4">{{ add_3_and_4 }}</span></td>
        <td></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>13</td>
        <td>Enter the amount from line 7</td>
        <td><span data-field="amount_from_line_7">{{ amount_from_line_7 }}</span></td>
        <td></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>14</td>
        <td>Enter the larger of line 11 or line 12</td>
        <td><span data-field="larger_of_11_or_12">{{ larger_of_11_or_12 }}</span></td>
        <td></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>15</td>
        <td>Subtract line 14 from line 13</td>
        <td><span data-field="subtraction_14_from_13">{{ subtraction_14_from_13 }}</span></td>
        <td></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>16</td>
        <td>2006 credit carryforward to 2008. Enter the smaller of line 6 or line 15</td>
        <td><span data-field="carryforward_2006_to_2008">{{ carryforward_2006_to_2008 }}</span></td>
        <td></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>17</td>
        <td>Subtract line 16 from line 15</td>
        <td><span data-field="subtraction_16_from_15">{{ subtraction_16_from_15 }}</span></td>
        <td></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>18</td>
        <td>2005 credit carryforward to 2008. Enter the smaller of line 5 or line 17</td>
        <td><span data-field="carryforward_2005_to_2008">{{ carryforward_2005_to_2008 }}</span></td>
        <td></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>19</td>
        <td>2007 credit carryforward to 2008. Subtract line 11 from line 3. If zero or less, enter -0.</td>
        <td><span data-field="carryforward_2007_to_2008">{{ carryforward_2007_to_2008 }}</span></td>
        <td></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td></td>
        <td>For Paperwork Reduction Act Notice, see back of form.</td>
        <td>Cat. No. 62502X</td>
        <td>Form 8396 (2007)</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start;">
    <div style="font-size: 12pt;">General Instructions</div>
    <div style="text-align: right; font-size: 12pt;">Page 2</div>
  </div>

  <h3 style="font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 15px;">Purpose of Form</h3>
  <p class="instruction">Use Form 8396 to figure the mortgage interest credit for 2007 and any credit carryforward to 2008.</p>

  <h3 style="font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 25px;">Who May Claim the Credit</h3>
  <p class="instruction">You may claim the credit only if you were issued a qualified mortgage credit certificate (MCC) by a state or local governmental unit or agency that issued a qualified mortgage credit certificate program.</p>

  <h3 style="font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 25px;">Certificates issued by the Federal Housing Administration, Department of Veterans Affairs, and Homestead Staff Certification do not qualify for the credit.</h3>

  <h3 style="font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 25px;">To whom the home to which the certificate relates must be your main home and also must be located in the jurisdiction of the governmental unit that issued the certificate.</h3>

  <h3 style="font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 25px;">If the interest on the mortgage was paid to a related person, you cannot claim the credit.</h3>

  <h3 style="font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 25px;">Refinanced Mortgage</h3>
  <p class="instruction">You can refinance your mortgage and still claim the credit if your existing MCC is revised and the resulting certificate meets all of the following requirements:</p>
  <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px;">
    <li>It must be issued to the holder(s) of the existing certificate for the same property.</li>
    <li>It must entirely replace the existing certificate.</li>
    <li>The portion of the outstanding balance of the existing certificate.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3 style="font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 25px;">Line 2</h3>
  <p class="instruction">The certificate credit rate cannot be less than 10% or more than 50%.</p>

  <h3 style="font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 25px;">If you refinanced, see Refinanced Mortgage on this page.</h3>

  <h3 style="font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 25px;">Receipt of Credit</h3>
  <p class="instruction">Enter the total of the amounts from Form 1040, lines 47 through 49 and lines 51 and 53; line 12 of the line 11 Worksheet in Pub. 972 (see instructions); and Form 5695, line 15</p>

  <h3 style="font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 25px;">Additional Information</h3>
  <p class="instruction">See Pub. 530, Tax Information for First-Time Homeowners, for more information.</p>

  <h3 style="font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 25px;">Specific Instructions</h3>
  <p class="instruction">Part I—Current Year Mortgage Interest Credit</p>
  <p class="instruction">Enter the interest you paid during the year on the loan amount (certified indebtedness amount) shown on your MCC. In most cases, this will be the amount shown on the MCC. If you have a mortgage interest statement, or an amortization schedule, you may use that to determine the interest paid. If the loan amount on your MCC is less than the loan amount on your MCC, see Pub. 530 for an example of how to allocate the interest.</p>

  <p class="instruction">Part II—Mortgage Interest Credit Carryforward to 2008</p>
  <p class="instruction">If the amount on line 11 is less than the amount on line 7, you may have an unused credit to carry forward to the next year. If you have an unused credit, you must use it first and then the prior year credits.</p>

  <p class="instruction">If you have any unused credit to carry forward, you must use it in the year you are filing for your credit for 2008.</p>

  <div class="caution">
    <p style="font-weight: bold;">CAUTION</p>
    <p>If you are subject to the $2,000 limit credit because your certificate credit rate is more than 20%, you may not be able to use the $2,000 limit for your prorated credit. See instructions for more information.</p>
  </div>

  <h3 style="font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 25px;">Paperwork Reduction Act Notice.</h3>
  <p class="instruction">This form is subject to the Paperwork Reduction Act. The United States. You are required to give us the information we need. It is to ensure that you are complying with the requirements of the Paperwork Reduction Act and collect the right amount of tax.</p>
</div>
</body>
</html>